But we have double quotes inside the href attribute value: the href value includes double quotes? Actually we have `href=\"data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg ...>\"`. The inner part includes `<svg ...>` which contains no double quotes, only single quotes. So fine.

Now game.js string: we need to escape double quotes inside the code. For example, in the code we have `const canvas = document.getElementById('gameCanvas');` which contains single quotes, fine. But there are double quotes in strings like `href=\"game.js\"`? Actually we have `<script src=\"game.js\" defer></script>` which includes double quotes around the filename; those need to be escaped as `\"`. Also in the code we have `gameOver`, `paused`, etc. Those are fine.

